<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany's 2027 budget: A record €561 billion and a mountain of debt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e8785ffa12c4d0bd46e5633e84612d0026ed37abf4078760d9555d14246266e</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-2027-budget-a-record-_561-billion-and-a-mountain-of-debt/a-79943216--747b01c10ad0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-2027-budget-a-record-€561-billion-and-a-mountain-of-debt/a-79943216?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2027 federal budget proposal has finally been hammered out and is set for a vote in parliament. What are the government's policy priorities in defense, infrastructure, the economy and social spending?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Parliament agrees on debt-laden 2027 budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:776287455e5a2a458f7d76a0640c870454b5b064656177cb8fbe4c188ab23c42</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-agrees-on-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-79936897--be62c4ec3578.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-agrees-on-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-79936897?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The budget committee in the Bundestag worked into the night to sign off on next year's spending plans. These include levels of new debt only eclipsed once, at the height of the COVID pandemic. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Could universal basic income be part of the solution in an AI economy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8fc518809769164d64c7a4a59bfc2b8a3e444aa5e9d395637ae9240802eb50b4</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T05:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-universal-basic-income-be-part-of-the-solution-in-an-ai-economy/a-79941597--51a6cced710b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-universal-basic-income-be-part-of-the-solution-in-an-ai-economy/a-79941597?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The scale of the economic disruption caused by AI has led even conservative politicians to talk about universal basic income. But economists are not convinced, and campaigners think we need to ask deeper questions.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Holzer Prize awarded to Katja Gloger and DW's Jaafar Abdul Karim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71f2bae0a9a38a05302e477820fc6ca6ce5111a1af9fd7d4b51ca26e3eb823b8</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T15:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-holzer-prize-awarded-to-katja-gloger-and-dw-s-jaafar-abdul-karim/a-79946916--5a434ad9f59c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-holzer-prize-awarded-to-katja-gloger-and-dw-s-jaafar-abdul-karim/a-79946916?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW journalist Jaafar Abdul Karim and Russia correspondent Katja Gloger have been awarded the prestigious Werner Holzer Prize for international journalism.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Wolf Biermann at 90: The singer who defied East Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61beefc4779f2eaf31276b325e7dcc53464a736bb36943d3dcd3c88088ffe898</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297--17726feda083.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">His life is a reflection of contemporary German history, which Biermann has addressed via his songs and sharp wit. Turning 90, he’s as feisty as ever.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Gen Z protests: Do Baby Boomers really have it better than young people?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8a3116dd9d7edcb4833e3e961840f7fcda30b5d4dbee5942f02e1f6b0650fa2</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854--e581c42657a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Should young people in Germany be more worried about their future than Baby Boomers were in the 1980s and 1990s? Or should both generations take to the streets and protest together? DW checked the data.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
